base64ToString(outputs('Get_file_content_using_path')?['body/$content'])



Set(
    varVtt,
    GetTranscript.Run(Substitute(locSelectedVideo.Name, ".mp4", ".vtt")).vtttext
);
ClearCollect(
    colCues,
    ForAll(
        MatchAll(
            Substitute(varVtt, Char(13), ""),
            "(?<h>\d+):(?<m>\d{2}):(?<s>\d{2}\.\d{3})\s*-->\s*(?<h2>\d+):(?<m2>\d{2}):(?<s2>\d{2}\.\d{3})[^\n]*\n(?<txt>[^\n]+)"
        ) As c,
        {
            StartSec: Value(c.h)*3600 + Value(c.m)*60 + Value(c.s),
            EndSec:   Value(c.h2)*3600 + Value(c.m2)*60 + Value(c.s2),
            CueText:  c.txt
        }
    )
);



"Cues: " & CountRows(colCues) & " | Chars: " & Len(varVtt)



Set(varNow, Video1.Time)




1. Timer (drives sync)

Insert → Input → Timer. Put on Selected Video screen.

Duration: 300
Repeat: true
AutoStart: true
Visible: false
OnTimerEnd:
Set(varNow, Video1.Time)
2. Transcript gallery

Insert → Blank vertical gallery. Place right of video or below.

Items:

Sort(colCues, StartSec, Ascending)

Gallery props:

TemplateSize: 60
ShowScrollbar: true

Insert one Label inside the gallery template:

Text: ThisItem.CueText
AutoHeight: true
Width: gallery width minus 30
Size: 12
Fill (highlight active line):
If(
    ThisItem.StartSec <= varNow && ThisItem.EndSec >= varNow,
    RGBA(0, 120, 212, 0.15),
    Color.Transparent
)
3. Click-to-seek

Gallery OnSelect:

Set(varSeek, ThisItem.StartSec);
Set(varReset, true);
Set(varReset, false)

On Video1:

StartTime: varSeek
Reset: varReset
